That may be the point; gzip compresses stuff, tar sticks stuff together.
If it's just a gzipped file, chances are it's just one file that's been
compressed. I'm not familiar with the patch, but if it's a patch it's
likely to be a file suitable for usage with diff - try opening the one
file that can't be broken down any further in notepad. You'll probably
find it's got code snippets inside. At this point you want to find a
program to apply diff patches in Windows, and apply it to the source, but
someone who knows more about what they're talking about can probably help
